//? Title: Warnsdorff's Rule: A Fast Knight Tour Is Still a Heuristic
//? Subtitle: Observable degree choices, starting-square failures and a permutation of handwritten-digit pixels
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
Warnsdorff's rule extends a knight path towards the unvisited neighbour
with the fewest onward moves. We derive its local choice and linear work
bound on a rectangular board, while distinguishing a valid path from a
complete or closed tour. The exact coordinate tie policy completes 61 of
64 starts on an 8 by 8 board; retained failure prefixes explain what the
older complete-or-empty API concealed. A completed tour then reorders the
64 measurements of each image in `dm::datasets::digits()`. Pixel values
and sums are preserved, but adjacent-value variation changes: a geometric
coverage heuristic does not optimise image smoothness.
)

\toc

> The data: numeric images on an 8 by 8 grid

The built-in digits frame contains 1797 handwritten images, each with
64 integer measurements between zero and sixteen and an original digit
label. Pixel columns are stored in row-major order. Remove `digit` when
forming a grid: the class label is not a sixty-fifth pixel. No model is
fitted to the labels in this report; they are used only for descriptive
grouping. The tour used below is fixed by board geometry and its start,
independently of every image's values.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/warnsdorff_data.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  const auto digits = dm::datasets::digits(); auto columns = digits.columns();
  columns.erase(std::remove(columns.begin(),columns.end(),"digit"),columns.end());
  std::print("{}\n",digits.select({"digit","pixel_0","pixel_27","pixel_28"}).head(6).to_md());
  auto summary = dm::algorithms::knight_tour_grid_summary(digits,columns,dm::algorithms::warnsdorff_attempt(8,8));
  summary.add_column("digit",digits.get_column("digit").values());
  std::print("\n{}\n",(summary | dm::group_by("digit") | dm::summarise(dm::agg::n("images"),
      dm::agg::mean("value_sum","mean_total_intensity"),dm::agg::sd("value_sum","sd_total_intensity"))).to_md(4));
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  dm::graphics::RPlot::hist(summary.get_column("value_sum").values(),30,"images")
      .title("Digits: sums of 64 quantised pixel intensities")
      .x_label("sum of pixel values").y_label("images")
      .size(1000,480).save_svg("build/warnsdorff_data.svg");
}
```
